# TODO - Complete bibliography

## Objective

Complete the repository bibliography so every material external claim,
toolchain,
platform, language, library, standard, legal authority, and research source has
one canonical, dated, uncertainty-aware provenance record.

## Acceptance

- Every external source cited by technical, research, legal, and publication
  documents resolves to one canonical bibliography record.
- Coverage includes the actual compiler, VM, accelerator, verification,
  interoperability, packaging, and publication dependencies used by the project.
- Empty taxonomy categories remain empty unless a real repository dependency or
  cited authority justifies a record; completeness is not simulated with filler.
- Duplicate source identities, stale versions, missing retrieval dates, weak
  secondary sourcing, broken links, and uncataloged material claims are audited
  and corrected.
- Primary or authoritative sources are preferred, while uncertainty,
  contradictions, and unresolved version or licensing questions remain visible.
- The coverage ledger and validator fail closed when a required record, citation
  target, source identity, or provenance field disappears.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Final validator output: `bibliography valid: 47 records, 44 baseline records,
  9 validation packages, 17 durable references`.
- The audit scans material URLs outside the bibliography and open planning
  records, normalizes Git transport suffixes, and rejects uncataloged durable
  references.
- Stable source identifiers are unique across all records; duplicate identities
  fail closed.
- Python 3.14.6 validation packages and standalone uv 0.11.16 are pinned to
  canonical records, and legacy pip is absent from the managed environment.
- Tooling schemas, museum-program provenance, host runtimes, compiler/toolchain
  identities, accelerator sources, standards, publications, and methodology
  records are represented in the closed taxonomy.
- Jig validates local links, catalogs, profiles, authored text, and lifecycle
  state without network access.

**Completion:** Completed on 2026-08-05 after the durable-reference inventory,
dependency-pin coverage, identity uniqueness checks, bibliography tests, and
repository-wide Jig validation passed without diagnostics.
